@startuml render_groups_presentation
title Render Groups -- presentation / delivery surface\nFour kinds of source trigger group state; each should be a thin adapter over ONE use-case.\nGroup status is never set directly -- it is a ROLLUP recomputed at one chokepoint: ReconcileGroupStatus.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classBackgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 70
left to right direction

' =================== SOURCES : who triggers group state ===================
package "1 - User commands   (desktop app -> HTTP)" as USER #c7d2fe {
  class "api/routers/render_groups.py" as RGR {
    POST /render-groups/create
    POST /render-groups/ID/confirm-upload
    POST /render-groups/ID/cancel
    POST /render-groups/cancel-all
    DELETE /render-groups/ID
    POST /render-groups/ID/multipart-upload/*
  }
  class "api/routers/jobs.py  (user)" as JRU {
    POST /jobs/ID/retry
  }
}

package "2 - Worker callbacks   (render machines -> HTTP)" as WORK #fde2c7 {
  class "api/routers/jobs.py  (worker)" as JRW {
    PUT  /jobs/ID/worker-start
    PUT  /jobs/ID/status      (running or failed)
    PUT  /jobs/ID/progress
    POST /jobs/ID/register-outputs
    PUT  /jobs/ID/heartbeat
    PUT  /jobs/ID/telemetry
    POST /jobs/ID/agent-failure
  }
}

package "3 - System daemons   (in-process trigger, NOT http)" as SYS #fbcfe8 {
  class "FleetMonitor tick" as MON {
    detects JobCounts.is_complete
    natural terminal -> reconcile
  }
  class "api/routers/internal.py" as INT {
    POST /internal/orphan/ID
    backup monitor -- dead heartbeat
  }
}

package "4 - Queries   (reads, no state change)" as READ #d1fae5 {
  class "render_groups.py  (read side)" as RGRr {
    GET /render-groups           list
    GET /render-groups/ID        + /status
    GET /render-groups/ID/outputs
    GET /render-groups/ID/download-zip
    GET /render-groups/ID/cost/estimate
    GET /render-groups/ID/pending-queue
  }
  class "api/routers/admin_dashboard.py" as ADM {
    GET /render-groups/active
    GET /jobs/active
  }
}

' =================== USE CASES : the application boundary ===================
package "Use Cases   (application layer)" as UC #d8f5d0 {
  class "RenderGroupService" as SVC {
    create()  confirm_upload()
    cancel()  delete()
    get_status()  list_with_status_page()
    get_outputs()  download_all_as_zip()
  }
  class "JobService" as JSVC {
    worker_start()  update_status()
    update_progress()  register_outputs()
    heartbeat()  retry()
  }
  class "Lifecycle = ReconcileGroupStatus\nthe ONE state-transition chokepoint" as LIFE {
    reconcile_group_status()
    write_terminal_snapshot()
  }
}

' =================== adapter -> use-case ===================
RGR  --> SVC   : command
JRU  --> JSVC  : command
JRW  --> JSVC  : chunk callback
INT  --> JSVC  : fail chunk
MON  --> LIFE  : reconcile
RGRr --> SVC   : read
ADM  --> SVC   : read

' =================== the rollup : chunk change -> group reconcile ===================
JSVC ..> LIFE  : chunk state changes;\nmonitor rolls up into group
SVC  ..> LIFE  : cancel / terminal ->\nwrite snapshot

note as NKEY #eef2ff
  The reframe
  ==
  * "Presentation" is NOT "HTTP". The FleetMonitor tick is a
    presentation-layer TRIGGER too -- a non-HTTP delivery
    mechanism into the same use-case (ReconcileGroupStatus).
  * No source sets group.status directly. A worker changes a
    CHUNK; a daemon reconciles the group. State is derived and
    eventually-consistent -- that is where the complexity lives.
end note

note as NLEAK #fee2e2
  Presentation leaks to close (render groups)
  ==
  * POST /render-groups/cancel-all runs a raw SQL query INSIDE
    the controller -> move to RenderGroupService.cancel_all_active().
  * GET .../cost/estimate and .../pending-queue shape the
    response DTO inline in the router -> use a presenter.
  * jobs.py worker callbacks do multi-step orchestration inline
    -> each should delegate to exactly one use-case.
end note

@enduml
